Open MOD files from the desktop: pt2-clone loads the module named on
its command line.  The icon is installed as pt2-clone.png: an icon name
with spaces makes gtk-update-icon-cache reject the whole hicolor cache.

Upstream status: offered upstream (https://github.com/8bitbubsy/pt2-clone/pull/54)

diff --git a/release/other/Freedesktop.org Resources/ProTracker 2 clone.desktop b/release/other/Freedesktop.org Resources/ProTracker 2 clone.desktop
--- a/release/other/Freedesktop.org Resources/ProTracker 2 clone.desktop	
+++ b/release/other/Freedesktop.org Resources/ProTracker 2 clone.desktop	
@@ -4,9 +4,10 @@ Type=Application
 Name=ProTracker 2 clone
 Name[fr]=Clone de ProTracker 2
 Comment=
-Exec=pt2-clone
-Icon=ProTracker 2 clone
+Exec=pt2-clone %f
+Icon=pt2-clone
 Path=
 Terminal=false
 StartupNotify=false
 Categories=AudioVideo;Audio;AudioVideoEditing;Sequencer;
+MimeType=audio/x-mod;
